{"text": "DRAFT v3 -- attorney work product -- do not file\n\nUNITED STATES DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE, EXECUTIVE\nOFFICE FOR IMMIGRATION REVIEW\nImmigration Court, Fort Snelling, Minnesota\n\nIn the Matter of: YOHANNES TESFAYE GEBREMARIAM, Respondent\n\nFile No. A 216-554-908\n\nIn removal proceedings\n\nDECLARATION OF RESPONDENT IN SUPPORT OF MOTION TO\nREOPEN AND RESCIND IN ABSENTIA ORDER\nI, Yohannes Tesfaye Gebremariam, declare as follows:\n\n1. I was born on 19 January 1987 in Adigrat. I am an Ethiopian national of\nTigrayan ethnicity and I belong to the Ethiopian Orthodox church. My first\nlanguage is Tigrinya. This declaration was read back to me in Tigrinya before I\nsigned it.\n\n2. I entered the United States at San Ysidro on 03/02/2022 and asked for asylum the\nsame day. I travelled on Ethiopian passport no. EP5530917. My Form I-589 was\nfiled within one year.\n\n3. I live at 1904 South 6th Street, Unit 12, Minneapolis, MN 55454. Since May 2023 I\nhave worked as a meat cutter at Northstar Halal Meats, Inc. under my\nemployment authorization, receipt number MSC2290417788.\n\n4. My former lawyer was Gerald P. Whitcombe of Whitcombe Immigration Law\nOffice, P.A. I paid Mr. Whitcombe $4,500 in cash over six visits. He gave me\nreceipts for only $3,000.\n\n5. Mr. Whitcombe never told me that my hearing had been moved up to August\n14, 2025. He did not file Form EOIR-33 when I moved, although I gave his office my\nnew address in writing. I was ordered removed in my absence. I first learned of\nthe order on Sept. 3, 2025, when my wife, Selamawit, opened a letter that had\nbeen forwarded from our old apartment in St. Paul.\n\n6. In my country I organized for an opposition student union and in 2021 I was\nheld for eleven days by federal police in Mekelle. I still have scars on both wrists\nfrom that time.\n\n7. I have been diagnosed with post-traumatic stress disorder. Since 11/18/2024 I\nhave been treated by Dr. Amina Warsame-Lindgren at Cedar-Riverside\nCommunity Health Center and I take sertraline 100 mg each morning. Dr.\nWarsame-Lindgren has written a letter, attached as Exhibit C.\n\n8. My daughter Liya was born in Minneapolis on 2023-06-11 and is a United States\ncitizen. She has a congenital heart defect and is followed by cardiology every\nthree months. Selamawit does not drive, and I take Liya to every appointment.\n\n9. On September 22, 2025 I filed a complaint against Mr. Whitcombe with the\nMinnesota Office of Lawyers Professional Responsibility, file no. OLPR-25-1147,\nand I mailed him a copy, as Matter of Lozada requires. He has not answered.\n\n10. I ask the Court to reopen my case under 8 C.F.R. § 1003.23(b)(4)(ii). I did not\nreceive notice, and I would never have missed my hearing on purpose.\n\nI declare under penalty of perjury under 28 U.S.C. § 1746 that the foregoing is true\nand correct. Executed at Minneapolis, Minnesota, on October 2, 2025.\n\n/s/ Y. T. Gebremariam\n\nCERTIFICATE OF INTERPRETATION\nI, Mulugeta Hailu, am fluent in Tigrinya and English and read this declaration to\nthe Respondent in Tigrinya. Hailu can be reached at 612 555 0119.\n\nCOUNSEL\nIngrid Sondergaard-Pham (Atty. ID MN 0398112)\n\nNorth Loop Immigrant Justice Clinic\n\n410 North 3rd Avenue, Suite 250, Minneapolis, MN 55401\n\nTel. (612) 555-0184\n\nisp@northloopijc.example", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 544 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Yohannes Tesfaye Gebremariam", "Gerald P. Whitcombe", "Selamawit", "Amina Warsame-Lindgren", "Liya", "Y. T. Gebremariam", "Mulugeta Hailu", "Ingrid Sondergaard-Pham"], "companies": ["United States DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE", "Executive Office for Immigration Review", "Northstar Halal Meats, Inc.", "Whitcombe Immigration Law Office", "St. Paul", "Cedar-Riverside Community Health Center", "Minnesota Office of Lawyers Professional Responsibility", "North Loop Immigrant Justice Clinic"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 147.80000000074506, "modelMs": 0, "detectors": ["email"